course: dictionary
lesson: 7456
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pop is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning is right. Your context clues tell you which one to use.
explain: Read this: «The beetle fires a boiling puff with a pop.» Here a pop is a short, sharp sound. Now read: «Mrs Hughes from next door pops round to check on her.» Here pop means to go somewhere quickly. Same word, different job.
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. A pop round to check on someone means a quick visit, so it fits. A pop sound fits the beetle sentence too. If it does not fit, try another meaning.
fact: Pop can be a verb: to burst with a short, sharp sound. A popped balloon is gone.
fact: Pop can be a noun: a pop is a short, sharp sound, like the pop of a cork.
fact: To pop somewhere means to go there quickly, as in «I'll pop to the shop.»
fact: Pop is also a fizzy sweet drink, also called soda, and a kind of music, as in «Western pop».
fact: Phrases such as «pop out», «pop in» and «pop up» each have their own meaning, so read the whole phrase, not just the first word.
exercise: «I'll pop to the shop.» What does pop mean here? | Burst with a bang | *Go there quickly | A kind of music | A fizzy drink
exercise: The balloon went pop. What happened to it? | It floated away into the sky | It turned into a drink | It grew bigger and bigger | *It burst with a short, sharp sound
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Mrs Hughes from next door pops round to check on her» that means makes a quick visit. | *pops | Hughes | next | check
test: «Singing styles differ around the world: Chinese folk and opera singing, Ukrainian folk singing and Western pop use the voice in different ways.» What is Western pop? | A short sharp sound | *A kind of music | Something that bursts | A fizzy drink
test: «The beetle fires a boiling puff with a pop.» What is a pop in this sentence? | A bright colour | *A short, sharp sound | A soft whisper | A long, slow sigh
exam: Which meaning of pop is a fizzy sweet drink? | Pop, to go somewhere quickly | Pop, to burst with a sound | *Pop, also called soda | Pop, a short sharp sound
